# Development-only working files.
#
# .probe/ is where the reverse-engineering evidence lives: extracted ROM art,
# video frames pulled from the original event's footage, and diffs against
# pret/pokegold.  It is how the port was worked out and it is worth keeping in
# the source tree, but it is Nintendo's material and it is no part of the mod,
# so it is never published.  (Both packers skip dotted directories wholesale,
# so this line is a guard against committing it, not against shipping it.)
.probe/

# Player-supplied art.  assets/ ships the how-to, not the picture: Celebi's
# descent sheet is a re-cut of the cart's own overworld graphic, so it is
# Nintendo's and is deliberately not in this repo -- which means a copy dropped
# in for local testing must not be committed either.  See assets/README.md.
assets/celebi.png

# Build output.  The release zip is built by CI from the tagged tree and
# attached to the GitHub Release; it is never committed.  See
# .github/workflows/release.yml, and README's "Releasing it".
*.modpkg
celebi_event-*.zip
celebi-event-*.zip
dist/

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
